mes_cli/profiles.py:1656`.\n- The behavior is covered by `tests/hermes_cli/test_profiles.py:1270`, which exports the default profile and imports it as a new profile while preserving config and memories.\n- User-facing docs describe the flow in `website/docs/reference/faq.md:760` for full-machine migration and `website/docs/reference/faq.md:782` for moving a single profile to another machine.\n\nThe broader unified cross-machine migration UX remains tracked separately in #6078 and the linked PRs, but the narrow \u201cexport/save as another computer profile\u201d path is already implemented.\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/4761156796/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]